thanks for your email. first, there is nothing special about lincombs
for one likelihood model or two likelihood model

the error says,

   Error in inla.lincomb section (file = file.ini, data.dir =
   data.dir, contr = cont.lincomb,   :
   lincomb lincomb.1 has only zero entries. This is not allowed

so you define a lincomb which is empty.

you do not give the whole formula, but you write

VEGTYPEB = the factor for the binary component

if you use

	~ ... + VEGTYPEB + ...

and its a factor, then this will expand to VEGTYPEB:<LEVELS> etc, so
that is the names you need to use in the lincomb

an alternative, is to use

	f(VEGTYPEB, model="iid",
		hyper = list(prec = list(initial = -3, fixed=TRUE))))

which will give a vector of results, and then the code above might
work.

be aware, that the factor as a fixed effect will remove a reference
level (like lm(), unless you request otherwise), which the f()
approach will not. maybe you need to add constr=T in the f().

let me know...

