Hi Tim,

This might not be a direct answer to your questions, but I can suggest a way to approach these problems.

1. Running INLA with int.strategy="eb", and the option to store the config
2. The latent posterior can be completely represented by the internal mode of the hyper-parameters, and the single precision matrix found in config
3. Store all the hyperpars and precision matrices across all models
4. Use the precision matrix of each model to generate samples when needed

Haakon

