Hi,

Thank you for your response.
I'm sorry, I was not very explicit in my previous message.

I have a varying-slope model with two likelihoods:

formulaHURDLE <- data ~ 0 + interceptB + interceptG + NDVIB +  NDVIG +
f(VEGTYPEB,NDVIB,model = 'iid') +
f(VEGTYPEG,NDVIG,model = 'iid') +
f(spde.index_mB, model = spde_m1) +
f(spde.index_mG, model = spde_m1)

So, I'm interested in computed the sums (B + b) and (G + g):

... + (B + b)*NDVIB + (G + b)*NDVIG +....

where b and g are the random effects.

Also, do you think it is advisable to add constr=T argument in f()? as you suggested in your message ...

Thank you!

Juanmi

